K5 the other exit: u_b a prescribed background (not varied). Then the baryons stay geodesic (div T_b = 0) while
   the P sector's Lagrangian J(|A_rel(t)|) depends explicitly on the prescribed flow; its energy changes at
   dE/dt = -dL/dt|explicit. In the reduced system with x_b(t) prescribed:
   the source the baryons would have felt (dL/dx_b'' = J'(y)) = a0*(g0 + Derivative(x_b(t), (t, 2)))/(K*(a0 + g0 + Derivative(x_b(t), (t, 2)))); nonzero unless y = 0, so the non-GR stress
   is not conserved and the Einstein equation's divergence (Bianchi: identically zero) cannot be matched: inconsistent.

K6 WEP.
   D: a compact free-falling body has A_rel = xddot + grad Phi = 0 inside it, so J'(0) = 0: no first-order force;
      but the free fall itself runs away at s = sqrt(4 pi G rho), a rate set by the body's density (K2):
      platinum: e-fold 235.8 s
      titanium: e-fold 514.3 s
